<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="151440" pluginName="Windows Print Spooler Remote Code Execution (PrintNightmare)" pluginFamily="Windows">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2022/05/03</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2021-34527</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>8.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The Print Spooler service on the remote host is affected by a remote code execution flaw. An authenticated user can install a malicious printer driver and run code as SYSTEM. On domain controllers this leads to domain compromise.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>151440.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Windows Print Spooler Remote Code Execution (PrintNightmare)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Print Spooler service : Running
RestrictDriverInstallationToAdministrators : not set
Point and Print NoWarningNoElevationOnInstall : 1</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-34527</see_also>
<solution>Apply the July 2021 (or later) cumulative update and set RestrictDriverInstallationToAdministrators = 1. Disable the Print Spooler service on domain controllers and any server that does not print.</solution>
<synopsis>The Print Spooler service on the remote host is affected by a remote code execution flaw.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="53" svc_name="dns" protocol="udp" severity="2" pluginID="12217" pluginName="DNS Server Cache Snooping Remote Information Disclosure" pluginFamily="DNS">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cvss3_base_score>5.3</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote DNS server answers non-recursive queries for domains it does not host. An attacker can find out which sites internal users have visited recently.</description>
<fname>12217.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>DNS Server Cache Snooping Remote Information Disclosure</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Nessus sent a non-recursive query for 'www.google.com' and received 1 answer from cache.</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<solution>Restrict recursion to internal clients and disable non-recursive answers from cache for external sources.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote DNS server answers non-recursive queries for domains it does not host.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
</ReportHost>
