<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="140657" pluginName="Netlogon Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability (Zerologon) (Remote)" pluginFamily="Windows">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2022/05/03</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2020-1472</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>10.0</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote domain controller is affected by an elevation of privilege flaw in the Netlogon Remote Protocol (MS-NRPC). An unauthenticated attacker with network access to the DC can establish a vulnerable Netlogon secure channel and set the computer account password of the domain controller, leading to full domain compromise.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>140657.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Netlogon Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability (Zerologon) (Remote)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Nessus was able to establish a Netlogon secure channel with an all-zero client credential
after 61 attempts.</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-1472</see_also>
<solution>Apply the August 2020 (or later) cumulative update and confirm that enforcement mode (FullSecureChannelProtection = 1) is enabled. Because RB-DC02 runs an unsupported OS, plan to demote and replace it with a supported domain controller.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote domain controller is affected by an elevation of privilege flaw in the Netlogon Remote Protocol (MS-NRPC).</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="0" svc_name="general" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="108797" pluginName="Unsupported Windows OS (remote)" pluginFamily="Windows">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cvss3_base_score>10.0</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote version of Microsoft Windows is either missing a service pack or is no longer supported. Lack of support implies that no new security patches for the product will be released by the vendor. Windows Server 2012 R2 reached end of extended support on October 10, 2023, and Windows Server 2008 R2 on January 14, 2020.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>108797.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Unsupported Windows OS (remote)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>RB-DC02    : Windows Server 2012 R2 Standard  (support ended 2023-10-10)
RB-HVAC-WS : Windows Server 2008 R2 Standard SP1 (support ended 2020-01-14)</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<solution>Upgrade to a supported version of Windows. If an upgrade is blocked by a vendor dependency (HVAC software), isolate the host on its own VLAN with an allow-list firewall policy until it is replaced.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote version of Microsoft Windows is either missing a service pack or is no longer supported.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
