<ReportItem port="8080" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="156014" pluginName="Apache Log4Shell RCE Detection via Path Enumeration (Direct Check)" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<agent>unix</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2021/12/24</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2021-44228</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>10.0</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote host has a version of Apache Log4j 2 earlier than 2.15.0 bundled with a Java application. JNDI features in configuration, log messages, and parameters do not protect against attacker-controlled LDAP and other JNDI endpoints. An unauthenticated attacker who can get a crafted string logged can execute arbitrary code.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>156014.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Apache Log4Shell RCE Detection via Path Enumeration (Direct Check)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Path              : /opt/workorder/lib/log4j-core-2.14.1.jar
Installed version : 2.14.1
Fixed version     : 2.17.1</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-44228</see_also>
<solution>Upgrade Apache Log4j to 2.17.1 or later (2.12.4 for Java 7, 2.3.2 for Java 6). If the vendor of the bundled application has not released a fixed build, remove the JndiLookup class from the classpath and restrict outbound LDAP/RMI from the server.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote host has a version of Apache Log4j 2 earlier than 2.15.0 bundled with a Java application.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="8080" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="233431" pluginName="Apache Tomcat 9.0.0.M1 &lt; 9.0.99 Partial PUT RCE" pluginFamily="Web Servers">
