<cisa-known-exploited>2025/04/22</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2025-24813</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>9.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The version of Apache Tomcat on the remote host is affected by a path equivalence flaw in partial PUT handling. When writes are enabled for the default servlet and file-based session persistence is in use, an attacker can upload a serialized payload and execute code.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>233431.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Apache Tomcat 9.0.0.M1 &lt; 9.0.99 Partial PUT RCE</plugin_name>
