<ReportItem port="22" svc_name="ssh" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="187315" pluginName="SSH Terrapin Prefix Truncation Weakness" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<agent>unix</agent>
<cve>CVE-2023-48795</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>5.9</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote SSH server supports ChaCha20-Poly1305 or CBC ciphers with Encrypt-then-MAC and does not support strict key exchange. A man-in-the-middle can drop messages at the start of the session and downgrade security features.</description>
<fname>187315.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>SSH Terrapin Prefix Truncation Weakness</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Supports following ChaCha20-Poly1305 Client to Server algorithm : chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com
Strict KEX : not supported</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-48795</see_also>
<solution>Update the SSH server to a release that supports strict KEX (OpenSSH 9.6 or vendor backport), or disable chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com and *-etm@openssh.com MACs.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote SSH server supports ChaCha20-Poly1305 or CBC ciphers with Encrypt-then-MAC and does not support strict key exchange.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
