<ReportItem port="9401" svc_name="unknown" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="207999" pluginName="Veeam Backup and Replication Deserialization RCE (KB4649)" pluginFamily="Windows">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2024/11/07</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2024-40711</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>9.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The version of Veeam Backup &amp; Replication installed on the remote host is affected by a deserialization of untrusted data flaw. An unauthenticated attacker can execute code on the backup server. This flaw has been used by ransomware operators to create local admin accounts and destroy backups before encryption.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>207999.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Veeam Backup and Replication Deserialization RCE (KB4649)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Path              : C:\Program Files\Veeam\Backup and Replication\
Installed version : 12.1.2.172
Fixed version     : 12.2.0.334</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-40711</see_also>
<solution>Upgrade Veeam Backup &amp; Replication to 12.2.0.334 or later. Remove the backup server from the domain or place it in a separate management tier, and keep at least one immutable or offline backup copy.</solution>
<synopsis>The version of Veeam Backup &amp; Replication installed on the remote host is affected by a deserialization of untrusted data flaw.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="57608" pluginName="SMB Signing not required" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cvss3_base_score>5.3</cvss3_base_score>
<description>Signing is not required on the remote SMB server. An unauthenticated attacker on the network can carry out man-in-the-middle and NTLM relay attacks against the SMB server.</description>
<fname>57608.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>SMB Signing not required</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Host does not require SMB signing (SMBv2 negotiate: signing enabled, not required).</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<solution>Enforce message signing with Group Policy: 'Microsoft network server: Digitally sign communications (always)' and the matching client setting. Test against copiers and older NAS devices first.</solution>
<synopsis>Signing is not required on the remote SMB server.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
