<ReportItem port="8040" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="190890" pluginName="ConnectWise ScreenConnect &lt; 23.9.8 Multiple Vulnerabilities" pluginFamily="CGI abuses">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2024/02/29</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2024-1709</cve>
<cve>CVE-2024-1708</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>10.0</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The version of ConnectWise ScreenConnect on the remote host is affected by an authentication bypass using an alternate path (SetupWizard.aspx). An unauthenticated attacker can create an administrator account and push code to every managed endpoint. A related path traversal flaw (CVE-2024-1708) allows code execution.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
