<ReportItem port="22" svc_name="ssh" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="201218" pluginName="OpenSSH &lt; 9.8 RCE (regreSSHion)" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<agent>unix</agent>
<cve>CVE-2024-6387</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>8.1</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The OpenSSH server on the remote host is affected by a signal handler race condition in sshd. An unauthenticated attacker may be able to execute code as root on glibc-based Linux systems. Exploitation takes many attempts but is practical.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>201218.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>OpenSSH &lt; 9.8 RCE (regreSSHion)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Banner            : SSH-2.0-OpenSSH_8.9p1 Ubuntu-3ubuntu0.6
Installed package : 1:8.9p1-3ubuntu0.6
Fixed package     : 1:8.9p1-3ubuntu0.10</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-6387</see_also>
<solution>Install the Ubuntu security update for openssh-server (1:8.9p1-3ubuntu0.10 or later on 22.04). If patching is delayed, set LoginGraceTime 0 in sshd_config and restrict tcp/22 to the IT management VLAN.</solution>
<synopsis>The OpenSSH server on the remote host is affected by a signal handler race condition in sshd.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="443" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="187100" pluginName="HTTP/2 Rapid Reset Denial of Service" pluginFamily="Web Servers">
<agent>unix</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2023/10/31</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2023-44487</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>7.5</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote web server supports HTTP/2 and is running a version affected by the Rapid Reset attack. A remote attacker can open and cancel streams at high rate and exhaust server resources, taking the public website offline.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>187100.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>HTTP/2 Rapid Reset Denial of Service</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Server header : nginx/1.18.0 (Ubuntu)
ALPN          : h2, http/1.1</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-44487</see_also>
<solution>Upgrade nginx to 1.25.3 or a distribution package that includes the fix, or set keepalive_requests and http2_max_concurrent_streams to conservative values. Upstream DDoS protection also mitigates this.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote web server supports HTTP/2 and is running a version affected by the Rapid Reset attack.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="22" svc_name="ssh" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="187315" pluginName="SSH Terrapin Prefix Truncation Weakness" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<agent>unix</agent>
<cve>CVE-2023-48795</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>5.9</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote SSH server supports ChaCha20-Poly1305 or CBC ciphers with Encrypt-then-MAC and does not support strict key exchange. A man-in-the-middle can drop messages at the start of the session and downgrade security features.</description>
<fname>187315.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>SSH Terrapin Prefix Truncation Weakness</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Supports following ChaCha20-Poly1305 Client to Server algorithm : chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com
Strict KEX : not supported</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-48795</see_also>
<solution>Update the SSH server to a release that supports strict KEX (OpenSSH 9.6 or vendor backport), or disable chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com and *-etm@openssh.com MACs.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote SSH server supports ChaCha20-Poly1305 or CBC ciphers with Encrypt-then-MAC and does not support strict key exchange.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
</ReportHost>
