<ReportItem port="3389" svc_name="msrdp" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="125313" pluginName="Microsoft RDP RCE (CVE-2019-0708) (BlueKeep) (uncredentialed check)" pluginFamily="Windows">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2022/05/03</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2019-0708</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>9.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote host is affected by a remote code execution vulnerability in Remote Desktop Services. An unauthenticated attacker can send specially crafted requests to the RDP service and execute arbitrary code. The flaw is wormable.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>125313.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Microsoft RDP RCE (CVE-2019-0708) (BlueKeep) (uncredentialed check)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Nessus detected the remote host is vulnerable by sending a crafted MS_T120 channel request.</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2019-0708</see_also>
<solution>Apply the May 2019 security update (KB4499175 / KB4499164 for Windows Server 2008 R2). Enable Network Level Authentication and block tcp/3389 from user VLANs. Move the HVAC console to a segmented building-systems VLAN.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote host is affected by a remote code execution vulnerability in Remote Desktop Services.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="0" svc_name="general" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="108797" pluginName="Unsupported Windows OS (remote)" pluginFamily="Windows">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cvss3_base_score>10.0</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote version of Microsoft Windows is either missing a service pack or is no longer supported. Lack of support implies that no new security patches for the product will be released by the vendor. Windows Server 2012 R2 reached end of extended support on October 10, 2023, and Windows Server 2008 R2 on January 14, 2020.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>108797.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Unsupported Windows OS (remote)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>RB-DC02    : Windows Server 2012 R2 Standard  (support ended 2023-10-10)
RB-HVAC-WS : Windows Server 2008 R2 Standard SP1 (support ended 2020-01-14)</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<solution>Upgrade to a supported version of Windows. If an upgrade is blocked by a vendor dependency (HVAC software), isolate the host on its own VLAN with an allow-list firewall policy until it is replaced.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote version of Microsoft Windows is either missing a service pack or is no longer supported.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="97833" pluginName="MS17-010: Security Update for Microsoft Windows SMB Server (ETERNALBLUE)" pluginFamily="Windows">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2022/08/10</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2017-0144</cve>
<cve>CVE-2017-0145</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>8.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote Windows host is affected by multiple remote code execution flaws in SMBv1. An unauthenticated attacker can execute code with a crafted packet. WannaCry and NotPetya used these flaws to spread.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>97833.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>MS17-010: Security Update for Microsoft Windows SMB Server (ETERNALBLUE)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Nessus sent a crafted SMBv1 transaction and received STATUS_INSUFF_SERVER_RESOURCES.</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2017-0144</see_also>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2017-0145</see_also>
<solution>Apply MS17-010 (KB4012212 for Windows Server 2008 R2) and disable SMBv1 (Set-SmbServerConfiguration -EnableSMB1Protocol $false).</solution>
<synopsis>The remote Windows host is affected by multiple remote code execution flaws in SMBv1.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="3389" svc_name="msrdp" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="42873" pluginName="SSL Medium Strength Cipher Suites Supported (SWEET32)" pluginFamily="General">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cve>CVE-2016-2183</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>7.5</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote host supports SSL ciphers that use 64-bit block ciphers (3DES). An attacker on the same network who can capture a long-lived session can recover plaintext with a birthday attack.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>42873.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>SSL Medium Strength Cipher Suites Supported (SWEET32)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Medium Strength Ciphers (&gt; 64-bit and &lt; 112-bit key, or 3DES)
  ECDHE-RSA-DES-CBC3-SHA   Kx=ECDH Au=RSA Enc=3DES-CBC(168) Mac=SHA1
  DES-CBC3-SHA             Kx=RSA  Au=RSA Enc=3DES-CBC(168) Mac=SHA1</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2016-2183</see_also>
<solution>Disable 3DES and other 64-bit block ciphers in the SChannel configuration (or application TLS settings) and allow only AES-GCM suites with TLS 1.2 or later.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote host supports SSL ciphers that use 64-bit block ciphers (3DES).</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="161" svc_name="snmp" protocol="udp" severity="3" pluginID="41028" pluginName="SNMP Agent Default Community Name (public)" pluginFamily="SNMP">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cve>CVE-1999-0517</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>7.5</cvss3_base_score>
<description>It is possible to obtain the default community name of the remote SNMP server. An attacker can read the device configuration, routing tables, and interface details, and on core-sw01 the community is read-write.</description>
