<description>The SSH server allows Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) encryption, which may let an attacker recover plaintext from the ciphertext under specific conditions.</description>
<fname>70658.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>SSH Server CBC Mode Ciphers Enabled</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>aes128-cbc
aes256-cbc
3des-cbc</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Low</risk_factor>
<solution>Disable CBC mode ciphers and allow CTR or GCM ciphers.</solution>
<synopsis>The SSH server allows Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) encryption, which may let an attacker recover plaintext from the ciphertext under specific conditions.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="80" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="1" pluginID="26194" pluginName="Web Server Transmits Cleartext Credentials" pluginFamily="Web Servers">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cvss3_base_score>2.6</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote web server contains a form with a password field that submits over plain HTTP. Credentials can be captured on the network.</description>
<fname>26194.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Web Server Transmits Cleartext Credentials</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Page : /admin/login.php
Destination : http://10.20.3.12/admin/auth.php</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Low</risk_factor>
<solution>Serve the login form and its target over HTTPS only, and redirect HTTP to HTTPS.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote web server contains a form with a password field that submits over plain HTTP.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="0" svc_name="general" protocol="icmp" severity="1" pluginID="10114" pluginName="ICMP Timestamp Request Remote Date Disclosure" pluginFamily="General">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cve>CVE-1999-0524</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>2.1</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote host answers ICMP timestamp requests, which lets an attacker learn the date set on the target. This can help defeat time-based authentication protocols.</description>
<fname>10114.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>ICMP Timestamp Request Remote Date Disclosure</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>The difference between the local and remote clocks is 2 seconds.</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Low</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-1999-0524</see_also>
<solution>Filter ICMP timestamp requests (13) and replies (14) at the host or network firewall.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote host answers ICMP timestamp requests, which lets an attacker learn the date set on the target.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
</ReportHost>
