<ReportItem port="80" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="200162" pluginName="PHP 8.1.x &lt; 8.1.29 CGI Argument Injection (Windows)" pluginFamily="CGI abuses">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2024/07/03</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2024-4577</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>9.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The PHP installation on this Windows host runs in CGI mode and is affected by an argument injection flaw caused by Windows 'Best-Fit' character conversion. An unauthenticated attacker can pass options to php-cgi and execute code. XAMPP default configurations are affected.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>200162.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>PHP 8.1.x &lt; 8.1.29 CGI Argument Injection (Windows)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Path              : C:\xampp\php\
Installed version : 8.1.10
Fixed version     : 8.1.29</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-4577</see_also>
<solution>Upgrade PHP to 8.1.29, 8.2.20, 8.3.8, or later. Better: move the class website to the district's managed web hosting and remove XAMPP from the workstation.</solution>
<synopsis>The PHP installation on this Windows host runs in CGI mode and is affected by an argument injection flaw caused by Windows 'Best-Fit' character conversion.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="80" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="11213" pluginName="HTTP TRACE / TRACK Methods Allowed" pluginFamily="Web Servers">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cvss3_base_score>5.3</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote web server supports the TRACE and/or TRACK methods, which echo the request back to the client and can expose headers such as cookies in cross-site tracing attacks.</description>
<fname>11213.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>HTTP TRACE / TRACK Methods Allowed</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>TRACE /Nessus123456.html HTTP/1.1 -&gt; HTTP/1.1 200 OK (request echoed)</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<solution>Disable TRACE and TRACK in the web server configuration (TraceEnable off for Apache).</solution>
<synopsis>The remote web server supports the TRACE and/or TRACK methods, which echo the request back to the client and can expose headers such as cookies in cross-site tracing attacks.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
