<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="268447" pluginName="Windows SMB Client Improper Access Control (October 2025)" pluginFamily="Windows : Microsoft Bulletins">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2025/11/10</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2025-33073</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>8.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote Windows host is missing a security update for the SMB client. An attacker who can coerce the host into authenticating to an attacker-controlled SMB server can reflect the authentication and gain SYSTEM privileges.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>268447.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Windows SMB Client Improper Access Control (October 2025)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>14 hosts missing KB5060842 or a later cumulative update. Oldest installed build: 22631.5262</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-33073</see_also>
<solution>Apply the June 2025 (or later) cumulative update and require SMB signing on clients and servers (see the 'SMB Signing not required' finding).</solution>
<synopsis>The remote Windows host is missing a security update for the SMB client.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="214985" pluginName="7-Zip &lt; 24.09 Mark-of-the-Web Bypass" pluginFamily="Windows">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2025/02/27</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2025-0411</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>7.0</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The version of 7-Zip on the remote host does not carry the Mark-of-the-Web to files extracted from a crafted nested archive. A phishing attachment can then run without SmartScreen or Office Protected View warnings.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>214985.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>7-Zip &lt; 24.09 Mark-of-the-Web Bypass</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Path              : C:\Program Files\7-Zip\
Installed versions: 19.00 (9 hosts), 22.01 (13 hosts)
Fixed version     : 24.09</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-0411</see_also>
<solution>Upgrade 7-Zip to 24.09 or later, or remove it and use the built-in Windows archive support. Deploy through Intune or SCCM; 7-Zip has no auto-update.</solution>
<synopsis>The version of 7-Zip on the remote host does not carry the Mark-of-the-Web to files extracted from a crafted nested archive.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="57608" pluginName="SMB Signing not required" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cvss3_base_score>5.3</cvss3_base_score>
<description>Signing is not required on the remote SMB server. An unauthenticated attacker on the network can carry out man-in-the-middle and NTLM relay attacks against the SMB server.</description>
<fname>57608.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>SMB Signing not required</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Host does not require SMB signing (SMBv2 negotiate: signing enabled, not required).</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<solution>Enforce message signing with Group Policy: 'Microsoft network server: Digitally sign communications (always)' and the matching client setting. Test against copiers and older NAS devices first.</solution>
<synopsis>Signing is not required on the remote SMB server.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
</ReportHost>
