<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="172529" pluginName="Security Updates for Microsoft Outlook (March 2023)" pluginFamily="Windows : Microsoft Bulletins">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2023/04/04</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2023-23397</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>9.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The Microsoft Outlook installation on the remote host is missing a security update. An attacker can send a message with an extended MAPI property containing a UNC path to an attacker-controlled SMB server. Outlook processes it on receipt, with no user interaction, and leaks the user's Net-NTLMv2 hash.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>172529.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Security Updates for Microsoft Outlook (March 2023)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Product           : Microsoft 365 Apps for enterprise (Semi-Annual Channel)
Installed build   : 16.0.15601.20526
Fixed build       : 16.0.15601.20578</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-23397</see_also>
<solution>Apply the March 2023 Office security updates through Microsoft 365 Apps update channels. Add users to the Protected Users group where possible and block outbound tcp/445 at the perimeter.</solution>
<synopsis>The Microsoft Outlook installation on the remote host is missing a security update.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
