<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="268447" pluginName="Windows SMB Client Improper Access Control (October 2025)" pluginFamily="Windows : Microsoft Bulletins">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2025/11/10</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2025-33073</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>8.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote Windows host is missing a security update for the SMB client. An attacker who can coerce the host into authenticating to an attacker-controlled SMB server can reflect the authentication and gain SYSTEM privileges.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>268447.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Windows SMB Client Improper Access Control (October 2025)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>14 hosts missing KB5060842 or a later cumulative update. Oldest installed build: 22631.5262</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-33073</see_also>
<solution>Apply the June 2025 (or later) cumulative update and require SMB signing on clients and servers (see the 'SMB Signing not required' finding).</solution>
<synopsis>The remote Windows host is missing a security update for the SMB client.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
