<description>Signing is not required on the remote SMB server. An unauthenticated attacker on the network can carry out man-in-the-middle and NTLM relay attacks against the SMB server.</description>
<fname>57608.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>SMB Signing not required</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Host does not require SMB signing (SMBv2 negotiate: signing enabled, not required).</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<solution>Enforce message signing with Group Policy: 'Microsoft network server: Digitally sign communications (always)' and the matching client setting. Test against copiers and older NAS devices first.</solution>
<synopsis>Signing is not required on the remote SMB server.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
</ReportHost>
