<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="241640" pluginName="RARLAB WinRAR &lt; 7.12 Directory Traversal" pluginFamily="Windows">
<agent>windows</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2025/12/30</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2025-6218</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>7.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The version of WinRAR on the remote host is affected by a directory traversal flaw. Extracting a crafted archive can write files outside the target folder, such as into the user's Startup folder, which leads to code execution at next logon.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>241640.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>RARLAB WinRAR &lt; 7.12 Directory Traversal</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Path              : C:\Program Files\WinRAR\
Installed version : 6.24
Fixed version     : 7.12</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-6218</see_also>
<solution>Upgrade WinRAR to 7.12 or later, or remove it from staff images if it is not licensed or required.</solution>
<synopsis>The version of WinRAR on the remote host is affected by a directory traversal flaw.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="445" svc_name="cifs" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="57608" pluginName="SMB Signing not required" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<agent>windows</agent>
