<ReportItem port="10443" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="190117" pluginName="Fortinet FortiOS SSL VPN Out-of-Bounds Write (FG-IR-24-015)" pluginFamily="Firewalls">
<agent>unix</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2024/02/16</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2024-21762</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>9.8</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The version of FortiOS running on the remote device is affected by an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the SSL VPN daemon (sslvpnd). A remote, unauthenticated attacker can execute arbitrary code or commands via specially crafted HTTP requests.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>190117.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Fortinet FortiOS SSL VPN Out-of-Bounds Write (FG-IR-24-015)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Installed version : 7.2.6
Fixed version     : 7.2.7
SSL VPN portal    : enabled (tcp/10443)</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-21762</see_also>
<solution>Upgrade FortiOS to 7.2.7 or later (7.4.3 or later on the 7.4 branch). If an immediate upgrade is not possible, disable SSL VPN; disabling the web-mode portal alone is not sufficient. Review the device for signs of compromise per Fortinet guidance before returning it to service.</solution>
<synopsis>The version of FortiOS running on the remote device is affected by an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the SSL VPN daemon (sslvpnd).</synopsis>
