<ReportItem port="443" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="183026" pluginName="Citrix NetScaler ADC and Gateway Information Disclosure (CTX579459) (Citrix Bleed)" pluginFamily="CGI abuses">
<agent>unix</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2023/11/08</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2023-4966</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>9.4</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote NetScaler appliance configured as a Gateway (VPN virtual server, ICA proxy, RDP proxy) is affected by a buffer over-read. An unauthenticated attacker can read memory that contains valid session tokens and hijack authenticated sessions, bypassing MFA.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>183026.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>Citrix NetScaler ADC and Gateway Information Disclosure (CTX579459) (Citrix Bleed)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Installed version : 13.1-48.47
Fixed version     : 13.1-49.15
Gateway vServer   : vdi_gw_vs (enabled)</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-4966</see_also>
<solution>Upgrade to NetScaler ADC 13.1-49.15 or later. After upgrading, kill all active and persistent sessions (kill icaconnection -all, kill aaa session -all, kill rdp connection -all, clear lb persistentSessions).</solution>
<synopsis>The remote NetScaler appliance configured as a Gateway (VPN virtual server, ICA proxy, RDP proxy) is affected by a buffer over-read.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
</ReportHost>
