<ReportItem port="443" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="4" pluginID="206797" pluginName="SonicWall SonicOS Improper Access Control (SNWLID-2024-0015)" pluginFamily="Firewalls">
<agent>unix</agent>
<cisa-known-exploited>2024/09/30</cisa-known-exploited>
<cve>CVE-2024-40766</cve>
<cvss3_base_score>9.3</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote SonicWall firewall is running a SonicOS version affected by an improper access control flaw in the management access and SSL VPN features. A remote attacker can gain unauthorized access to resources or crash the firewall. This flaw has been used for initial access in ransomware campaigns.</description>
<exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
<fname>206797.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>SonicWall SonicOS Improper Access Control (SNWLID-2024-0015)</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>Installed version : 7.0.1-5030
Fixed version     : 7.0.1-5035
WAN HTTPS management : enabled</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Critical</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-40766</see_also>
<solution>Upgrade SonicOS to 7.0.1-5035 or later on Gen 7 devices. Restrict management to trusted internal addresses, disable WAN management, reset passwords for all local SSL VPN users, and enforce MFA for SSL VPN.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote SonicWall firewall is running a SonicOS version affected by an improper access control flaw in the management access and SSL VPN features.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="443" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="104743" pluginName="TLS Version 1.0 Protocol Detection" pluginFamily="Service detection">
<agent>unix</agent>
<cvss3_base_score>6.5</cvss3_base_score>
<description>The remote service accepts connections encrypted using TLS 1.0, which has known design flaws. PCI DSS and most current guidance require disabling it.</description>
<fname>104743.nasl</fname>
<plugin_name>TLS Version 1.0 Protocol Detection</plugin_name>
<plugin_output>TLSv1.0 is enabled and the server supports at least one cipher.</plugin_output>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<solution>Disable TLS 1.0 and 1.1 and enable TLS 1.2 and 1.3. On Windows, set the SChannel protocol registry keys or use IIS Crypto; confirm SIS and finance integrations support TLS 1.2 first.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote service accepts connections encrypted using TLS 1.0, which has known design flaws.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
</ReportHost>
